        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Explains a Brightline Commercial consolidated invoice for a property group site by site: each site's services, charges and tax, the PO number, payment terms and due date, and capital project milestone invoices (deposit, installation, commissioning). Use it for property groups, their sites, and commercial contract or project invoices.</description>
        <developerName>RLM_HVAC_Commercial_Invoice_Questions</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Always call the Explain Commercial Invoice by Site action before answering. Pass currentRecordId as recordId whenever the user is on an Invoice or Account record, the property group or site name the user mentioned, the site they asked about as siteName, the invoice number if given, and any amount they mentioned as a number. Don't ask for the customer's name when currentRecordId is available.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Answer only from the action's explanation. Never calculate, estimate, round or change any amount, never split costs differently from the explanation, and never offer discounts or credits. If the explanation says no invoice or site matches, say so and describe the invoice it returned.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Lead with one sentence that answers the question, for example "Invoice DOC-000000007 is $4,551.13 for all seven Lakeshore sites under PO LPG-PO-2026-118, due Dec 5, 2026." Then give a short list with each site's total and its charges plus tax. If the user asked about one site, explain that site's services line by line and say what share of the invoice it is.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction3</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>For a capital project invoice, say which milestone it bills (deposit, installation or commissioning) and the share of the project. End by noting the invoice goes to accounts payable at headquarters with the PO number, so each site's subtotal can be allocated to that site's budget.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction4</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 4</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If you can't tell which property group the user means, ask for its name. Never show Salesforce record Ids; refer to invoices by their document number.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction5</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 5</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
